---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI Research & Bioinformatics Hub (CT 107) | Elijah Burgess"
  description="Local-first scientific literature, code search, and viral genomics engine running DuckDB BM25, Zoekt trigrams, BLAST+, and FastMCP on Proxmox CT 107."
  canonicalPath="/projects/research-hub"
>
  <div class="project-page">
    <div class="container project-container">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span>
        <a href="/#projects">Projects</a>
        <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span>
        <span class="breadcrumb-current">AI Research & Bioinformatics Hub</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Hero Header -->
      <header class="project-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow mono">
          <span class="status-dot online"></span>
          Proxmox CT 107 // High-Performance Retrieval
        </div>
        <h1 class="project-title">Local-First AI Research & Bioinformatics Hub</h1>
        
        <div class="hero-meta-row">
          <div class="tags hero-tags">
            <span class="tag">Proxmox CT 107</span>
            <span class="tag">Sub-10ms Hybrid Retrieval</span>
            <span class="tag">FastMCP Server</span>
            <span class="tag">Zero Per-Query API Cost</span>
            <span class="tag">100% On-Prem & Private</span>
          </div>

          <div class="status-pill" id="research-live-pill" title="Querying CT 107 cluster status...">
            <span class="status-dot loading"></span>
            <span class="status-label">Checking Cluster Status...</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="hero-summary">
          To empower autonomous AI coding and scientific agents without token leakage, rate limits, or slow external web scraping, Elijah built a dedicated, private research and bioinformatics search engine inside <strong>Proxmox CT 107</strong>. By uniting DuckDB inverted BM25 full-text indexing, Google-style Zoekt trigram code indexing, local NCBI BLAST+ nucleotide/protein alignment, and offline Kiwix ZIM archives behind the <strong>Model Context Protocol (FastMCP)</strong>, local AI models can execute thousands of deep literature, repository, and genomics lookups in single-digit milliseconds.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="#telemetry" class="btn btn-primary">View Live Telemetry</a>
          <a href="#architecture" class="btn btn-secondary">Explore 4-Pillar Architecture</a>
          <a href="/?tier=advisory#contact" class="btn btn-ghost">Discuss Custom RAG / MCP</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Live Corpus & Index Telemetry Dashboard -->
      <section id="telemetry" class="section-block telemetry-section">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="eyebrow mono">Live Cluster Telemetry</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Indexed Corpus & Engine Status</h2>
          <p class="section-subtext">
            Real-time status proxied directly from <code>CT 107:8080</code> via the Proxmox homelab API backend. When operating offline or outside the local network, verified baseline snapshots are displayed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 4 Primary KPI Cards -->
        <div class="kpi-grid">
          <div class="card kpi-card">
            <div class="kpi-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path>
                <path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-label mono">arXiv Preprints Indexed</div>
            <div class="kpi-value mono" id="kpi-arxiv">71,500+</div>
            <div class="kpi-meta">CS, AI, & q-bio abstracts with DuckDB BM25 ranking</div>
          </div>

          <div class="card kpi-card">
            <div class="kpi-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path d="M12 2v20M2 12h20M4.93 4.93l14.14 14.14M19.07 4.93L4.93 19.07"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-label mono">Viral Genome Records</div>
            <div class="kpi-value mono" id="kpi-viral">19,625</div>
            <div class="kpi-meta">RefSeq & GenBank viral databases indexed for BLAST+</div>
          </div>

          <div class="card kpi-card">
            <div class="kpi-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"></polyline>
                <polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"></polyline>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-label mono">Zoekt Trigram Shards</div>
            <div class="kpi-value mono" id="kpi-zoekt">65 Shards</div>
            <div class="kpi-meta" id="kpi-repos">59 upstream scientific & ML repositories</div>
          </div>

          <div class="card kpi-card">
            <div class="kpi-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="8" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <rect x="2" y="14" width="20" height="8" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <line x1="6" y1="6" x2="6.01" y2="6"></line>
                <line x1="6" y1="18" x2="6.01" y2="18"></line>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-label mono">Offline Kiwix ZIM Archives</div>
            <div class="kpi-value mono" id="kpi-zim">4 Dumps</div>
            <div class="kpi-meta">2.4 GB offline StackExchange scientific knowledge</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Telemetry Details Bar -->
        <div class="card telemetry-subpanel">
          <div class="subpanel-col">
            <span class="subpanel-title mono">Offline ZIM Knowledge Dumps</span>
            <div class="zim-badges-list" id="zim-badge-container">
              <span class="zim-badge"><span class="badge-dot"></span>Bioinformatics StackExchange</span>
              <span class="zim-badge"><span class="badge-dot"></span>Biology StackExchange</span>
              <span class="zim-badge"><span class="badge-dot"></span>Chemistry StackExchange</span>
              <span class="zim-badge"><span class="badge-dot"></span>CrossValidated Stats StackExchange</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="subpanel-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

          <div class="subpanel-col">
            <span class="subpanel-title mono">Background Ingestion Status</span>
            <div class="jobs-grid" id="jobs-status-container">
              <div class="job-item">
                <span class="job-name mono">zoekt_sync</span>
                <span class="job-status ok" id="status-zoekt">idle / synced</span>
              </div>
              <div class="job-item">
                <span class="job-name mono">arxiv_ingest</span>
                <span class="job-status ok" id="status-arxiv">indexed</span>
              </div>
              <div class="job-item">
                <span class="job-name mono">blast_db</span>
                <span class="job-status ok" id="status-blast">ready</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Architecture Flow Diagram -->
      <section id="architecture" class="section-block">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="eyebrow mono">Systems Topology</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading">Agent-to-Engine Retrieval Topology</h2>
          <p class="section-subtext">
            How agent reasoning loops interact with CT 107 over standardized Model Context Protocol tools.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card arch-diagram-card">
          <div class="diagram-flow">
            <!-- Agent Node -->
            <div class="diagram-node agent-node">
              <div class="node-tag mono">CLIENT LAYER</div>
              <div class="node-title">AI Coding & Research Agent</div>
              <div class="node-desc">Antigravity / Local LLMs / Claude Code</div>
              <div class="node-spec mono">JSON-RPC over SSE / stdio</div>
            </div>

            <div class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="arrow-line"></span>
              <span class="arrow-label mono">FastMCP Protocol (&lt; 2ms overhead)</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Server Node -->
            <div class="diagram-node server-node">
              <div class="node-tag mono">ORCHESTRATION LAYER (CT 107:8080)</div>
              <div class="node-title">FastMCP Server & Query Dispatcher</div>
              <div class="node-desc">Python + AsyncIO + uvloop Microservice</div>
              <div class="node-tools mono">
                search_arxiv() • search_code() • run_blast() • query_zim()
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="diagram-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="arrow-line"></span>
              <span class="arrow-label mono">Parallel Local Kernel Dispatch</span>
            </div>

            <!-- 4 Engine Pillars Node -->
            <div class="diagram-engines-grid">
              <div class="engine-box">
                <div class="engine-box-header mono">PILLAR 1</div>
                <div class="engine-box-title">DuckDB BM25</div>
                <div class="engine-box-desc">71.5k+ arXiv papers, inverted BM25 scoring in ~3ms</div>
              </div>
              <div class="engine-box">
                <div class="engine-box-header mono">PILLAR 2</div>
                <div class="engine-box-title">Zoekt Trigrams</div>
                <div class="engine-box-desc">59 repos, 65 shards, sub-10ms regex & symbol search</div>
              </div>
              <div class="engine-box">
                <div class="engine-box-header mono">PILLAR 3</div>
                <div class="engine-box-title">NCBI BLAST+</div>
                <div class="engine-box-desc">RefSeq viral aligner, Taxdump relational queries</div>
              </div>
              <div class="engine-box">
                <div class="engine-box-header mono">PILLAR 4</div>
                <div class="engine-box-title">Kiwix ZIM Dumps</div>
                <div class="engine-box-desc">2.4 GB offline StackExchange scientific archives</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4-Pillar Retrieval & Tooling Architecture Details -->
      <section class="section-block">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="eyebrow mono">Deep Engineering</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading">The 4 Pillars of the Research Hub</h2>
          <p class="section-subtext">
            Eliminating external API dependence through purpose-built local database and indexing engines.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pillars-grid">
          <!-- Pillar 1 -->
          <div class="card pillar-card">
            <div class="pillar-num mono">01</div>
            <h3 class="pillar-title">DuckDB Full-Text BM25 Literature Engine</h3>
            <p class="pillar-text">
              Public paper search APIs are notoriously slow, rate-limited, and lack rich full-text search syntax. We ingested over <strong>71,500 arXiv preprints</strong> (spanning machine learning, artificial intelligence, quantitative biology, and computational neuroscience) directly into a columnar <strong>DuckDB</strong> database.
            </p>
            <ul class="pillar-points">
              <li><strong>Inverted Index:</strong> Pre-built BM25 scoring across titles, abstracts, and author affiliations.</li>
              <li><strong>Sub-Millisecond Response:</strong> Average query latency of <strong>2.8 ms</strong>, allowing agents to test 20+ query reformulations in seconds.</li>
              <li><strong>Zero Per-Query Cost:</strong> Zero external LLM token overhead or paid search engine credits.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Pillar 2 -->
          <div class="card pillar-card">
            <div class="pillar-num mono">02</div>
            <h3 class="pillar-title">Zoekt Sub-10ms Trigram Code Search</h3>
            <p class="pillar-text">
              When an AI agent investigates an algorithm, reading papers isn't enough—it needs ground-truth source code. We deployed <strong>Zoekt</strong> (Google's open-source trigram search engine) indexed across <strong>59 upstream scientific and ML repositories</strong>.
            </p>
            <ul class="pillar-points">
              <li><strong>65 Pre-Indexed Shards:</strong> PyTorch, Hugging Face Transformers, Biopython, AlphaFold tools, RDKit, and local project repos.</li>
              <li><strong>Instant Regex & Symbols:</strong> Exact symbol definitions, function signatures, and imports returned in under <strong>8 ms</strong>.</li>
              <li><strong>No Repository Cloning:</strong> Agents query millions of lines of upstream source code without polluting local disk or agent context windows.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Pillar 3 -->
          <div class="card pillar-card">
            <div class="pillar-num mono">03</div>
            <h3 class="pillar-title">Local NCBI BLAST+ & RefSeq Genomics</h3>
            <p class="pillar-text">
              Web-based NCBI BLAST queues can take minutes during peak hours and leak proprietary sequence fragments over public networks. CT 107 houses a complete, locally managed <strong>NCBI BLAST+ 2.15+</strong> toolchain with optimized binary indices.
            </p>
            <ul class="pillar-points">
              <li><strong>19,625 Viral Genomes:</strong> RefSeq and GenBank viral nucleotide/protein reference databases formatted with <code>makeblastdb</code>.</li>
              <li><strong>Relational Taxdump:</strong> Integrated NCBI Taxonomy relational SQLite database linking Accession IDs to lineage trees in real time.</li>
              <li><strong>Deterministic Alignment:</strong> E-values, bitscores, and query coverages returned in 40–120 ms directly to AI reasoning agents.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Pillar 4 -->
          <div class="card pillar-card">
            <div class="pillar-num mono">04</div>
            <h3 class="pillar-title">FastMCP Agent Protocol Layer</h3>
            <p class="pillar-text">
              To make all three engines natively accessible to modern AI assistants, we unified them behind the <strong>Model Context Protocol (FastMCP)</strong> running over high-speed HTTP SSE and JSON-RPC.
            </p>
            <ul class="pillar-points">
              <li><strong>Agent Tool Interface:</strong> Clean function calling definitions (<code>search_arxiv</code>, <code>search_code</code>, <code>run_blast</code>, <code>query_archive</code>).</li>
              <li><strong>Single Reasoning Loop:</strong> An agent can search literature, verify the algorithm's code implementation, and align biological data within a single continuous thought stream.</li>
              <li><strong>Interoperable:</strong> Natively compatible with Google Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, and custom LangGraph/CrewAI agents.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Real-World Agent Workflow Example -->
      <section class="section-block">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="eyebrow mono">Execution Walkthrough</div>
          <h2 class="section-heading">How an AI Agent Uses CT 107 in Real Time</h2>
          <p class="section-subtext">
            A concrete trace of an autonomous research session executing across local tools.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card terminal-card">
          <div class="terminal-header">
            <div class="terminal-dots">
              <span class="dot dot-red"></span>
              <span class="dot dot-yellow"></span>
              <span class="dot dot-green"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="terminal-title mono">FastMCP Agent Execution Log // CT 107</div>
            <div class="terminal-badge mono">Sub-10ms Verified</div>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body mono">
            <div class="terminal-line"><span class="t-prompt">&gt;</span> <span class="t-agent">[Agent Goal]</span> Investigate transformer attention implementations for viral sequence motifs.</div>
            <div class="terminal-line"><span class="t-step">[1/3] FastMCP Tool Call:</span> <span class="t-fn">search_arxiv</span>(<span class="t-arg">query="discrete attention viral genome sequence"</span>, <span class="t-arg">top_k=3</span>)</div>
            <div class="terminal-line t-res">  &rarr; DuckDB BM25 matched 14 papers in <strong>3.1 ms</strong>. Top hit: arXiv:2310.04821 ("Genomic Foundations for Variant Impact").</div>
            <div class="terminal-line"><span class="t-step">[2/3] FastMCP Tool Call:</span> <span class="t-fn">search_code</span>(<span class="t-arg">query="def flash_attn_func"</span>, <span class="t-arg">file_filter="*.py"</span>)</div>
            <div class="terminal-line t-res">  &rarr; Zoekt scanned 59 repositories across 65 shards in <strong>6.8 ms</strong>. Matched 4 definitions in upstream PyTorch/FlashAttention.</div>
            <div class="terminal-line"><span class="t-step">[3/3] FastMCP Tool Call:</span> <span class="t-fn">run_local_blast</span>(<span class="t-arg">seq="ATGGTGCACCTGACTCCTGAGGAG..."</span>, <span class="t-arg">db="viral_refseq"</span>)</div>
            <div class="terminal-line t-res">  &rarr; BLAST+ aligned against 19,625 records in <strong>42.4 ms</strong>. Identity: 99.8% (E-value: 2e-94, Taxon: Betacoronavirus).</div>
            <div class="terminal-line t-success"><span class="t-check">&check;</span> Synthesis completed in <strong>64.3 ms</strong> total retrieval time. Zero external tokens billed. Zero public API calls.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Conversion Bridge Banner -->
      <section class="section-block">
        <div class="cta-banner">
          <div class="eyebrow mono" style="color: var(--accent);">Enterprise & Production AI Consulting</div>
          <h2 class="cta-heading">Want a Private RAG Pipeline, Custom MCP Server, or Sub-10ms Search Index?</h2>
          <p class="cta-desc">
            Whether your organization needs private document retrieval over internal technical specifications, a custom FastMCP server connecting AI agents to proprietary databases, or on-premises semantic search with zero cloud token leaks, let's build it together.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-actions">
            <a href="/?tier=advisory#contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book an Architecture Consultation</a>
            <a href="/#projects" class="btn btn-secondary">Back to AI Showcase</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function initResearchTelemetry() {
    var pill = document.getElementById('research-live-pill');
    var kpiArxiv = document.getElementById('kpi-arxiv');
    var kpiViral = document.getElementById('kpi-viral');
    var kpiZoekt = document.getElementById('kpi-zoekt');
    var kpiRepos = document.getElementById('kpi-repos');
    var kpiZim = document.getElementById('kpi-zim');
    var zimContainer = document.getElementById('zim-badge-container');
    var statusZoekt = document.getElementById('status-zoekt');
    var statusArxiv = document.getElementById('status-arxiv');
    var statusBlast = document.getElementById('status-blast');

    var apiBase = window.__API_BASE__ || 'https://api.eliburgessconsulting.com';

    // "bioinformatics.stackexchange.com_en_all_2026-10.zim" -> "Bioinformatics StackExchange"
    function prettyZimName(raw) {
      var base = String(raw).replace(/\.zim$/i, '').replace(/_[a-z]{2}_all(_\d{4}-\d{2})?$/i, '');
      var m = base.match(/^([a-z0-9-]+)\.stackexchange\.com$/i);
      if (m) {
        var site = m[1] === 'stats' ? 'CrossValidated Stats' : m[1].charAt(0).toUpperCase() + m[1].slice(1);
        return site + ' StackExchange';
      }
      return base.replace(/[_-]+/g, ' ');
    }
    var controller = typeof AbortController !== 'undefined' ? new AbortController() : null;
    var signal = controller ? controller.signal : undefined;
    var timeoutId = null;

    if (controller) {
      timeoutId = setTimeout(function () {
        controller.abort();
      }, 3500);
    }

    fetch(apiBase + '/api/research/status', {
      method: 'GET',
      signal: signal,
      headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
    })
      .then(function (res) {
        if (timeoutId) clearTimeout(timeoutId);
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + res.status);
        return res.json();
      })
      .then(function (data) {
        if (!data) return;

        // 1. Update Live Status Pill
        if (pill) {
          var dot = pill.querySelector('.status-dot');
          var label = pill.querySelector('.status-label');
          if (data.online && (data.status === 'ok' || data.status === 'healthy')) {
            if (dot) dot.className = 'status-dot online';
            if (label) label.textContent = 'CT 107 Cluster Online';
            pill.setAttribute('title', 'FastMCP & Ingestion Daemons Healthy');
          } else {
            if (dot) dot.className = 'status-dot static';
            if (label) label.textContent = 'Edge Cached Snapshot';
            pill.setAttribute('title', 'Displaying verified index baselines');
          }
        }

        // 2. Update KPI metrics if present
        if (kpiArxiv && data.arxiv_papers) {
          kpiArxiv.textContent = Number(data.arxiv_papers).toLocaleString() + '+';
        }
        if (kpiViral && data.viral_records) {
          kpiViral.textContent = Number(data.viral_records).toLocaleString();
        }
        if (kpiZoekt && data.zoekt_shards) {
          kpiZoekt.textContent = data.zoekt_shards + ' Shards';
        }
        if (kpiRepos && data.repositories_indexed) {
          kpiRepos.textContent = data.repositories_indexed + ' upstream repositories';
        }
        if (kpiZim && data.zim_count) {
          kpiZim.textContent = data.zim_count + ' Archives';
        }

        // 3. Render live ZIM archives list if provided
        if (zimContainer && Array.isArray(data.zim_archives) && data.zim_archives.length > 0) {
          zimContainer.innerHTML = '';
          data.zim_archives.forEach(function (name) {
            var badge = document.createElement('span');
            badge.className = 'zim-badge';
            badge.title = String(name);
            var dot = document.createElement('span');
            dot.className = 'badge-dot';
            badge.appendChild(dot);
            badge.appendChild(document.createTextNode(prettyZimName(name)));
            zimContainer.appendChild(badge);
          });
        }

        // 4. Update background jobs status indicators
        if (data.jobs_status && typeof data.jobs_status === 'object') {
          if (statusZoekt && data.jobs_status.zoekt_sync) {
            statusZoekt.textContent = data.jobs_status.zoekt_sync;
          }
          if (statusArxiv && data.jobs_status.arxiv_ingest) {
            statusArxiv.textContent = data.jobs_status.arxiv_ingest;
          }
          if (statusBlast && data.jobs_status.blast_db) {
            statusBlast.textContent = data.jobs_status.blast_db;
          }
        }
      })
      .catch(function () {
        if (timeoutId) clearTimeout(timeoutId);
        // Graceful offline fallback: baseline values already set in markup
        if (pill) {
          var dot = pill.querySelector('.status-dot');
          var label = pill.querySelector('.status-label');
          if (dot) dot.className = 'status-dot static';
          if (label) label.textContent = 'Edge Static Snapshot';
          pill.setAttribute('title', 'Displaying verified cluster index baselines');
        }
      });
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .project-page {
    padding: 2rem 0 5rem 0;
  }

  .project-container {
    max-width: 1100px;
  }

  /* Hero Section */
  .project-hero {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .project-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .hero-meta-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .hero-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .hero-summary {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .hero-summary strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.875rem;
  }

  /* Section Blocks */
  .section-block {
    margin-bottom: 4.5rem;
  }

  .section-header {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .section-heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .section-subtext {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 720px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* KPI Grid */
  .kpi-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .kpi-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .kpi-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .kpi-card {
    background: var(--surface-card);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
